      en: "Wat Sri Chum is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Thailand. A temple in Sukhothai Historical Park housing a massive, 15-meter tall seated Buddha statue called 'Phra Achana' inside a cubical mandapa. Phra Achana means 'one who is not frightened'. A legend says the statue once spoke to soldiers to encourage them. The walls have a secret passage. This site holds particular significance in the history of Thailand, from the Sukhothai and Ayutthaya kingdoms to modern Bangkok. Like many notable places in Thailand, it combines regional character with the legacy of the Chao Phraya, the Mekong and Buddhist tradition. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Thailand, between the Andaman coast, rice paddies and tropical forests.",
